# Project Architecture Rules

This project combines two previous Godot projects into one clean game.

The new project under `godot_game/` is authoritative.

The donor projects are reference material only:

* `donor_projects/board_game_M13/` contains the previous board-game prototype.
* `donor_projects/KF_wizard_game/` contains the previous wizard/duel/embodied prototype.

Do not copy donor projects wholesale.
Inspect donor projects and migrate only useful, understood pieces.

## Game identity

The game is a hybrid of:

* Catan-style economy;
* Pandemic-style threat spread;
* Seven Wonders-style city development;
* optional embodied wizard/hero gameplay.

The strategic board game is the source of truth.

The embodied wizard game is an optional way to experience or resolve board events.

## Core board model

Hexes are resource producers.

Catan corner spaces are `BoardNode`s.

`BoardNode`s are also Pandemic-style locations.

Edges connect `BoardNode`s.

Roads are built on edges.

Cities are built on `BoardNode`s.

Heroes and demons exist on `BoardNode`s as generic macro pieces/counters.

Macro hero-vs-demon contact is **instant deterministic resolution** (hero removes all demons on node). This is **not** tactical spell combat.

Underworld/demon spread uses a Pandemic-style infection deck (design intent); tactical combat uses `SpellCombatSession` in isolated modes and future 3D encounters only.

The legacy `CombatResolver` card-duel model is debug/reference.

Development cards are built into cities and may unlock board effects, embodied effects, or both.

## Folder responsibilities

`godot_game/core/`

* Headless deterministic game engine.
* Owns GameState, board state, rules, actions, events, bots, scoring, simulation, and seeded randomness.
* Must not depend on UI, scenes, Node3D, input, physics, animation, rendering, or the live scene tree.

`godot_game/embodied/`

* 3D/player/wizard/hero gameplay.
* May contain CharacterBody3D, Node3D, input, camera, movement, animations, and embodied encounter scenes.
* Must not directly mutate authoritative game state.

`godot_game/integration/`

* Translates between core board state and embodied scenes.
* Maps BoardNodes to world anchors.
* Applies embodied encounter results back through core rules.

`godot_game/ui/`

* Debug UI, board UI, combat UI, menus, logs, and presentation.

`godot_game/tests/`

* Headless tests for core rules and deterministic simulation.
* Integration tests where appropriate.

## Determinism

Same seed plus same action sequence must produce the same state and event log.

All randomness in `core/` must go through a controlled RNG wrapper.

Do not use global random functions directly in core rules.

## Rule design

Rules mutate `GameState` explicitly.

Rules should return `GameEvent`s describing what happened.

UI/embodied code may request actions but must not directly edit:

* resources;
* city ownership;
* road ownership;
* demon count;
* hero location;
* scores;
* underworld deck;
* win/loss state.

## Testing

Prefer tests before implementation.

Do not delete, weaken, skip, or rewrite tests merely to make progress.

Each milestone should include acceptance tests.

Core tests must be runnable without opening gameplay scenes.

## Cursor workflow

Work milestone by milestone.

**Read first:** `docs/RULEBOOK.md`, `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md`, `docs/TESTING_AND_GIT_WORKFLOW.md`, `docs/NEXT_MILESTONES.md`, `docs/RULES_ENGINE_AUDIT.md`.

Before coding a milestone:

1. Restate the milestone goal.
2. List expected files to change.
3. List tests to add or update.
4. State what is explicitly out of scope.

After coding:

1. Run the relevant tests.
2. Summarise changed files.
3. Summarise new/updated tests.
4. Report test result.
5. Note remaining risks.
6. Suggest a Git commit message.

Do not continue into the next milestone without review.

## Do not do

Do not merge both donor projects in one pass.

Do not make KF economy/world code authoritative.

Do not put UI, Node3D, CharacterBody3D, physics, input, or rendering code inside `core/`.

Do not let UI, integration, embodied, or run-mode scripts directly mutate `GameState` (resources, cities, roads, demons, heroes, scores, win/loss).

Do not build a full drafting/development-card system before human playable 2D/strategic interaction exists (unless explicitly requested).

Do not wire tactical spell combat (`SpellCombatSession`) into the macro economy loop.

Do not use legacy card-duel (`CombatResolver`) as v1 macro hero/demon resolution.

Do not build ports or Catan-style fixed trade ratios.

Do not create a second parallel GameState.
